        "Integrity mechanisms answer particular questions. A hash can detect a change relative to a trustworthy expected digest, but an attacker who replaces both data and unprotected digest can defeat that comparison. A signature or independently protected append record adds different guarantees and key-management obligations. None of these establishes that every original event was generated or that an attacker did not omit events before signing."
