      "What does authenticated encrypted transport primarily protect?|The collection connection|Truth of every source claim~A compromised source can send false data over a protected connection.|Generation of every event~Transport does not force an application to emit missing events.|Unlimited queue durability~A protected connection does not establish persistent buffering.|Transport protection secures the channel under its assumptions, not the completeness or truth of source events.",
      "Which key best identifies retry copies of one event?|Stable event ID|Actor identifier alone~One actor can perform many distinct actions.|Source hostname alone~A host produces many unrelated events.|Minute timestamp alone~Different events can occur within the same minute.|A stable event identity distinguishes repeated delivery of one observation from separate observations.",
